<title>USA: TABLE-Besicorp Q1 shr $0.35 vs $0.14.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Besicorp Q1 shr $0.35 vs $0.14.</headline>
<dateline>KINGSTON, N.Y. 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended June 30,</p>
<p>					     1997		     1996</p>
<p> Revenues			   $4,961,956	     $3,647,358</p>
<p> Net Income			  1,027,701		  403,909</p>
<p> Income per Common Share		 .35			.14</p>
<p>Weighted Average Number of</p>
<p>Shares Outstanding (in Thousands)</p>
<p>					     2,935		    2,912</p>
<p>NOTE: Michael J. Daley, vice-president and chief financial officer, said, &quot;The increase in net income for the quarter ended June 30, 1997 is primarily due to the company's Project Development business which recorded income from partnerships of $2,746,608 during the quarter compared to $2,004,491 for the three months ended June 30, 1996, and development and management fees of $727,527 compared to $146,033 for the comparable prior period.  Due to the nature of the Project Development business, the company's results of operations may fluctuate significantly from quarter to quarter.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
